  "version": "1.4.0",
  "changelog": "The cache + Apply workflow: opening a piece loads it once into a working copy, and nothing is sent back while you work \u2014 drags, point edits and renames all stay in the editor until you press Apply, which sends that piece's edits to GitHub in one verified round trip. Switching pieces, closing a tab, opening a piece another editor sent, or quitting with unapplied edits now asks Apply / Discard / Stay \u2014 nothing is saved silently (switching used to save on its own) and nothing is lost silently. A page with unapplied edits wears a bullet on its tab, and the window title says so. Buildings work exactly the same way.",
